WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.184
Last Thursday, just before dinner, Steve Jones and his sister were playing in their front yard.

2
00:00:08.185 --> 00:00:13.844
It was a warm spring day and they were enjoying themselves in the sun.

3
00:00:13.845 --> 00:00:21.295
All of a sudden, the sky started to get dark. Then it became even darker.

4
00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:26.459
"It looks like it's going to rain," said Steve. "We'd better get inside."

5
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.431
Just then the wind really started to blow.

6
00:00:30.432 --> 00:00:36.419
As the children reached their house, a large lightning bolt struck nearby.

7
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:43.452
Then they heard thunder boom. Within minutes it was raining very hard.

8
00:00:43.453 --> 00:00:48.584
"This is the biggest thunderstorm I have ever seen!" exclaimed Steve.

9
00:00:48.585 --> 00:00:50.867
"Look! Now it's snowing!"

10
00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:54.498
"That's not snow," said Steve's dad.

11
00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:57.821
"That's hail. We'd better turn on the radio.

12
00:00:57.822 --> 00:01:01.266
There might be a tornado coming."

13
00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:09.308
"The National Weather Service has issued a tornado warning for Madison County in Texas," said the voice on the radio.

14
00:01:09.309 --> 00:01:11.991
"This could really be a bad one.

15
00:01:11.992 --> 00:01:17.203
You'd better move to a small room in your house and get away from any windows.

16
00:01:17.204 --> 00:01:21.475
If you have a basement, go downstairs right now."

17
00:01:21.476 --> 00:01:23.425
Then came the wind.

18
00:01:23.426 --> 00:01:29.515
It roared so loudly that Steve thought a train was driving through their kitchen.

19
00:01:29.516 --> 00:01:35.190
Dad had to shout at the top of his lungs to tell the family what to do.

20
00:01:35.191 --> 00:01:39.007
"Everyone! Go to the basement now!" he shouted.

21
00:01:39.008 --> 00:01:44.101
Dad turned off the electricity and Steve turned off the gas.

22
00:01:44.102 --> 00:01:47.590
Then the family hid in the basement.

23
00:01:47.591 --> 00:01:53.166
The noise grew louder and louder. Then the house started to shake.

24
00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:59.401
They could hear the glass smashing and wood breaking. It was terrifying.

25
00:01:59.402 --> 00:02:02.492
Steve and his sister started to cry.

26
00:02:02.493 --> 00:02:06.132
"What's going on?" Steve shouted.

27
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:10.251
"The tornado is hitting our house!" Dad shouted.

28
00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:14.302
"Don't move! Cover your head with your hands."

29
00:02:14.303 --> 00:02:21.437
After a few terrible minutes, the sound quieted down and the house stopped shaking.

30
00:02:21.438 --> 00:02:26.118
Steve and his family carefully climbed out of their basement.

31
00:02:26.119 --> 00:02:28.854
Their house was a complete mess.

32
00:02:28.855 --> 00:02:36.418
All of the windows had been smashed to pieces, and things had been blown all over the house.

33
00:02:36.419 --> 00:02:39.843
Outside, things were just as bad.

34
00:02:39.844 --> 00:02:46.390
The family car was upside down, and most of their trees had been knocked down.

35
00:02:46.391 --> 00:02:52.363
Debris was scattered all over the neighborhood. Steve started to cry.

36
00:02:52.364 --> 00:02:57.412
"Everything we own is gone," cried Steve.

37
00:02:57.413 --> 00:03:01.847
But Steve's dad replied, "That's not true, Steve.

38
00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:09.381
We're all alive and safe, and that's what is most important."

39
00:03:09.382 --> 00:03:14.782
Tornadoes are very powerful and can cause great destruction.

40
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:21.802
When warm, moist air collides with cold, dry air, the air does not mix well.

41
00:03:21.803 --> 00:03:27.567
If warm air gets trapped below the cold air, it tries to push itself up.

42
00:03:27.568 --> 00:03:34.948
As the warm air moves upward, it spins around extremely quickly.

43
00:03:34.949 --> 00:03:39.484
The mixing of cold air and warm air causes a thunderstorm.

44
00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:46.679
Usually the thunderstorm just dies out, but sometimes the air rotation is very strong.

45
00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:55.895
Most tornadoes are very small and don't cause much damage, but some tornadoes can be very dangerous.

46
00:03:55.896 --> 00:04:01.360
There are three kinds of tornadoes: weak, strong, and violent.

47
00:04:01.361 --> 00:04:09.602
A weak tornado will not hurt you if you are inside your house, but a strong tornado can be very harmful.

48
00:04:09.603 --> 00:04:15.586
However, if you are in the basement of your house, you will probably be okay.

49
00:04:15.587 --> 00:04:20.655
Violent tornadoes are the worst. They are the real killers.

50
00:04:20.656 --> 00:04:26.305
Even if you are in your basement, you may not be safe from one of them.

51
00:04:26.306 --> 00:04:30.167
The tornado that hit Steve's house was a strong one.

52
00:04:30.168 --> 00:04:35.295
The wind twisting inside it was about two hundred kilometers an hour.

53
00:04:35.296 --> 00:04:39.172
That is twice as fast as a car drives on the highway.

54
00:04:39.173 --> 00:04:50.474
Steve and his family are alive and safe today because they listened to the tornado warning and took refuge in their basement.

55
00:04:50.475 --> 00:04:59.529
After several weeks of hard work, Steve's family managed to repair their house and return to their usual life.

56
00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:05.434
But Steve never forgot the day when the tornado hit his house.

